  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The family and the demonstrative",
   "texto": [
    "To present the people of the family we use «Dit is...» (this / this is) or «Dat is...» (that / that is). To ask about someone's identity: «Wie is...?» (Who is...?). It notes the gender and articles of family members: «de vader» (the father), «de moeder» (the mother), «de broer» (the brother), «de zus» (the sister), «de man» (the man / husband), «de vrouw» (the wife / wife), «de ouders» (the parents), and in neutral genus «het kind» (the child / son)."
   ]
  },
